  "specId": "318-explicit-task-render-context",
  "issue": 414,
  "request": "GitHub Issue #414. Goal: Explicitly validate task identity and context for spec render, resolving audit findings F-007 and F-023 while guaranteeing output-path confinement and target-spec context consistency. Scope: src/flow/schemas/spec.schema.json, src/spec/commands/render.js, src/flow/lib/render-spec-view.js, and src/flow/lib/sync-spec-tasks.js. Acceptance: TaskId enforces schema character and length constraints and rejects separators, traversal, and absolute-path-equivalent input; TaskCollection rejects duplicate IDs and unknown parents; TaskOutputPath rejects resolution outside the target directory before any write; SpecRenderContext reads only metadata colocated with the specified spec; render, view, and sync require validated value objects; all rejection paths have no side effects; add failing reproductions before implementation and automated proof without direct test mutation of flow state or artifacts; preserve successful paths and sync docs when source changes. Out of scope: unrelated audit findings, npm publish, npm dist-tag, and official release. Parallel constraint: serialize changes touching src/spec/commands/render.js with CI or Node support work.",
